{"connection_id": "BC-c05207aca2d4e6d9a0c1", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.1.14", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "writer expects to lay aside his body", "note": "The writer says his bodily dwelling will soon be put off, immediately before promising enduring remembrance; the bequest of teaching is motivated by expected death."}
{"connection_id": "BC-384eb2321a4ae72eda97", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.1.15", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remembrance after death", "note": "The speaker will ensure that his addressees can recall his teaching after his departure; this is a direct Christian formulation of advice preserved as a legacy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c5613fabe32455411acc", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.1.15", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remember teaching after my departure", "note": "Expecting his departure, the writer promises to enable continued remembrance afterward; instruction deliberately survives the speaker's death."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9258704b324ce57a0a1d", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remember prophets and apostolic command", "note": "Readers are to remember the words spoken by holy prophets and the Lord's command through apostles; the charge crosses a chain of messengers and remains active in its hearers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5249ecfd58db1b4c7830", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.2.15", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hold received traditions", "note": "Believers are told to stand firm and hold traditions taught orally or by letter; the commentary's inherited charge is preserved in two concrete channels."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4e6869a82ab9cbdea2e2", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.1.14", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "good deposit", "note": "The writer tells Timothy to guard the good deposit entrusted to him; this makes the commentary's image of a delivered amanah into a specific charge to preserve teaching."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e369959854f1350928b5", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.1.14", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "guard the good deposit", "note": "Timothy is told to guard an entrusted good deposit through the Holy Spirit; the commentary's bequeathed instruction is explicitly treated as something in custody."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e12c8520e93f6379c7a", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.1.5", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith inherited from grandmother and mother", "note": "Timothy's sincere faith is remembered as having lived first in his grandmother Lois and mother Eunice; this is a named household chain for the commentary's bequeathed belief."}
{"connection_id": "BC-aab4c1a35ec41f6a723e", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "witnessed teaching passed onward", "note": "Timothy is to entrust what he heard before many witnesses to faithful people able to teach others; the four-stage chain concretely develops the commentary's counsel handed from one generation to another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd73b8a05e17c23ea192", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "entrust teaching to teachers of others", "note": "What Timothy heard before witnesses is to be entrusted to faithful people able to teach others; testimony, faithful custody and another generation of speakers coincide."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ef40a63cbb735d037c87", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.3.14", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "continuing in received teaching", "note": "Timothy is told to continue in what he learned and believed, knowing from whom he learned it; this explicitly links faith to a trustworthy chain of teachers, as the commentary links faith to counsel passed onward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a0e6006b223f1e8def8e", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.3.14", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "continue in learning received from others", "note": "Timothy is told to continue in what he learned, knowing the people from whom he learned it; the received charge depends on identifiable transmitters and continued practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ca2a70752c68cf50261c", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.3.15", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "scripture known since childhood", "note": "Timothy has known the sacred writings from infancy, and they can make him wise for salvation; the inherited word is a specific text learned before adulthood."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc07b9667a25575cf4a1", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhortation with patience", "note": "In the final charge before the writer speaks of his approaching death, Timothy is told to correct, rebuke, and exhort with complete patience and teaching; this directly pairs the commentary's mutual counsel with ṣabr."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6a033163f5e5b1c68268", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort with patience and teaching", "note": "Timothy is charged to reprove, rebuke and exhort with complete patience and teaching; the commentary's linked counsel and endurance are applied to instruction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9c4bfd9a4e74be18a79e", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.5", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance in a final charge", "note": "The writer tells Timothy to endure hardship and fulfill his ministry; read with the letter's imminent-death statement, it is a concrete last charge that carries steadfast service forward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dbcbd505bd5ff766eb0c", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.6", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speaker's approaching death", "note": "The writer says he is already being poured out and that the time of departure has come; this supplies an explicit deathbed frame for the succession and deposit language elsewhere in the letter."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5de1b66732a4decdcd10", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.6", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Paul's approaching departure", "note": "Paul describes himself as being poured out and his departure near; the surrounding charge to Timothy becomes a deliberate word handed on before death."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2ed6feb7dc82d655b1a5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.10.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "prayers and alms remembered together", "note": "Cornelius is told his prayers and alms have ascended before God; the two practices paired in the commentary's speech of Jesus are joined in a remembered disciple's life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d71fdf66e332a35c247e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.20.25", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "farewell to a community", "note": "Paul tells the Ephesian elders that they will see his face no more; this establishes the farewell setting for his entrusting them with teaching and inheritance in the next part of the speech."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec468cfffeae7731cd84", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.20.29", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "danger after Paul's departure", "note": "Paul says destructive wolves will enter after he leaves; the farewell charge anticipates dangers the recipients must meet when the original speaker is gone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-31638e9f634359d8b9e1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.20.31", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remember prolonged admonition", "note": "Paul tells elders to stay alert and remember that he admonished each with tears for three years; the departing teacher leaves a remembered practice of warning."}

