{"connection_id": "BC-29962387adc0d4f7dee8", "ref": "Tobit 4:3", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "father's final instruction", "note": "Tobit tells his son, as his own death approaches, to bury him and not neglect his mother; this Jewish deathbed charge gives the commentary's image of a father's bequest to the living a concrete family setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-44e6df6fea8b84ab1186", "ref": "Tobit 4:3", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "dying father's instructions to his son", "note": "Believing he may die, Tobit calls Tobias and charges him to bury him and care for his mother; a dying speaker gives a son concrete duties to perform afterward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d90c2d70e7be1d6eaf7d", "ref": "WLC:1Chr.22.13", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "father links obedience and courage", "note": "David tells Solomon he will prosper if he observes the statutes given through Moses and urges him to be strong, courageous and unafraid; inherited law is paired with fortitude."}
{"connection_id": "BC-01e23449205426c1b3b7", "ref": "WLC:1Chr.28.9", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "David charges Solomon to know his father's God", "note": "David tells his son Solomon to know the God of his father and serve him wholeheartedly; the commentary's inherited worship and practical instruction meet in a father's direct charge."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9eab2b0e066a459dfbfc", "ref": "WLC:1Kgs.2.1", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "David charges Solomon before dying", "note": "When David's death draws near he gives Solomon a charge; this is a royal deathbed instance of instruction left to someone who must act after the speaker."}
{"connection_id": "BC-34b587d0d8d24d953c0c", "ref": "WLC:1Kgs.2.2", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "deathbed testament", "note": "David announces that he is going the way of all the earth and addresses Solomon before dying; the scene supplies the explicit farewell frame implied by the commentary's image of counsel as a bequest."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f965c22d02cfd41330e0", "ref": "WLC:1Kgs.2.3", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "charge to successor", "note": "David charges Solomon to keep God's commandments and walk in God's ways; this is a father's binding instruction to the successor who will carry his obligations forward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dc7b1462c2de3e924d3b", "ref": "WLC:1Kgs.2.3", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "David's charge to keep statutes", "note": "David tells Solomon to keep God's charge and walk in his ways; the inherited instruction has religious practice, rather than property alone, as its subject."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d8a1d145b719436ea1d9", "ref": "WLC:1Kgs.8.31", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "oath before the altar", "note": "A person accused by a neighbor comes to swear before God's altar; the commentary likewise places a disputed oath after communal worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b02732eaddd41f6f602f", "ref": "WLC:1Kgs.8.32", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "vindicate the righteous under oath", "note": "Solomon asks God to judge the sworn dispute and vindicate the righteous; this specifies the concern for a truer testimony when a first oath is suspect."}
