{"connection_id": "BC-60be6ada85751e0bf8eb", "ref": "WLC:Deut.32.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ʾ-m-n / Hebrew ʾ-m-n; package table's sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary labels ءَامَنُوا۟ with Arabic root ʾ-m-n; Deuteronomy joins Hebrew אֱמוּנָה, faithfulness, with God's justice and uprightness, bringing the commentary's adjacent faith and al-ḥaqq together while leaving the sound-based cognacy unverified."}
{"connection_id": "BC-858c441d0f2afb0f9cbd", "ref": "WLC:Deut.32.46", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "command children to obey all the words", "note": "Moses tells Israel to set its heart on his warning and command its children to observe the law; the dying generation actively passes an obligation to the next."}
{"connection_id": "BC-02d83f4c6630b0b15ed5", "ref": "WLC:Deut.32.47", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "transmitted words are life", "note": "Moses says the commanded word is no empty thing but Israel's life, by which their days in the land will be prolonged; the inherited counsel has an explicitly future consequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-eb08101305246d481960", "ref": "WLC:Deut.4.40", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "חקק sound correspondence; statutes and descendants", "note": "Israel must keep God's statutes so that it goes well with them and their children after them; the table's חקק correspondence joins prescribed duty to the commentary's bequest across generations."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cef42df103e55341c79d", "ref": "WLC:Deut.6.20", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "חקק sound correspondence; child asks about statutes", "note": "A child asks what the Lord's decrees mean, prompting parental explanation; חֻקִּים from the table's חקק correspondence turns prescribed right into transmitted teaching."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2e0394227428d99d9982", "ref": "WLC:Deut.6.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teach the words to children", "note": "Israel is told to repeat the commanded words to its children in daily settings; counsel becomes a continuing intergenerational duty like the commentary's inherited recommendation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f570ec683b1ed365c292", "ref": "WLC:Deut.7.9", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ʾ-m-n / Hebrew ʾ-m-n; package table's sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary labels ءَامَنُوا۟ with Arabic root ʾ-m-n; Deuteronomy calls God הָאֵל הַנֶּאֱמָן, faithful and covenant-keeping to a thousand generations, connecting belief with fidelity that survives across generations while leaving cognacy unproven."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ee1554a15297027adcaa", "ref": "WLC:Deut.7.9", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "אמנ sound correspondence; faithful covenant keeper", "note": "God is called faithful and keeps covenant and loyalty with those who love and obey him to a thousand generations; the table's אמנ family joins trustworthiness to a long inherited obligation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a1add6327a667758a0a0", "ref": "WLC:Eccl.9.12", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "people do not know their time", "note": "Like fish in a net and birds in a snare, people are caught by sudden calamity; it makes concrete the commentary's warning that death may arrive before a bequest can be made."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0cc5ccdecbd0872e5bd0", "ref": "WLC:Esth.8.8", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "irrevocable writing", "note": "The commentary calls the will binding, while the source lexicon's ʿ-ṣ-r (B006) gloss also evokes retracting a gift; Esther's sealed royal writing cannot be revoked, so redress requires a new counter-decree rather than withdrawal."}

