{"connection_id": "BC-4bd5fcc3493738d4fede", "ref": "WLC:Ps.105.10", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "חקק sound correspondence; decree to Jacob", "note": "God confirms the promise to Jacob as a statute and enduring covenant; Hebrew חֹק from the table's חקק correspondence joins fixed obligation to the patriarchal chain."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d8de1f78328f91972bd1", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.122", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God asked to stand surety", "note": "The psalmist asks God to be surety for the servant's good against oppressors; the commentary's kefil image extends here from a human promisor to divine protection."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cd859131c4a5c48d6882", "ref": "WLC:Ps.15.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "vow kept despite personal cost", "note": "The commentary's Arabic lexicon gloss for root ʿ-ṣ-r (B006) describes giving a gift and then withdrawing it; Psalm 15 praises the person who swears to their own hurt and does not change, a direct counter-image of retracting one's word."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2198c8a365681c6c866c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.15.4", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "oath honored even at personal cost", "note": "The person fit to dwell with God swears to his own hurt and does not change his word; it clarifies the weight of the commentary's binding oath when keeping it becomes burdensome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c22271089548679c4e7f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.2.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ḥ-q-q / Hebrew ḥ-q-q; package table's sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary labels بِٱلْحَقّ with Arabic root ḥ-q-q and describes a binding right; the Hebrew king announces a חֹק, a decree, from the candidate root חקק, so the psalm shows a related legal sense without proving cognacy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-71e065072bc9ca20698d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.2.7", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "חקק sound correspondence; decree given to a son", "note": "The king recites the Lord's decree declaring him a son; Hebrew חֹק from the table connects a prescribed word to a father-son relation, though it is a royal oracle rather than an inheritance allotment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-07bd80fbe7f3f2f2b9d3", "ref": "WLC:Ps.2.8", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "son receives an inheritance", "note": "The royal son is promised the nations as his inheritance; this develops the commentary's image of a binding grant passing from a father to an heir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-385fc51ad88f1c93997b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.37.34", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wait patiently and keep the way", "note": "The psalm calls its hearer to wait for the Lord and keep his way amid the wicked's apparent success; obedience and endurance are joined as in the commentary's final counsel."}
