{"connection_id": "BC-b372906d7ac8b93262e8", "ref": "WLC:Zech.8.16", "target": "sec10", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic ʾ-m-n / Hebrew ʾ-m-n; package table's sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary labels ءَامَنُوا۟ with Arabic root ʾ-m-n and بِٱلْحَقّ with ḥ-q-q; Zechariah uses אֱמֶת from Hebrew root ʾ-m-n in a command to speak truth neighbor to neighbor, giving the faith/truth words a concrete communal setting while leaving cognacy unproven."}
